From 1cb43fff0052c5be809b8ab5a44a24865f99c6d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:47:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media-driver: Add 415 more missing include dirs
 (comprehensive sweep)

A real build failed with a fatal "'media_debug_interface.h' file not
found" compiling vp_debug_interface.cpp -- a core shared file, not
limited to the "_base" platform variants fixed in the previous
commit. That fix only addressed a narrow slice of a much larger
Android.bp generator gap.

Did a full sweep: every directory under media_common/, media_driver/,
media_softlet/, and cmrtlib/ containing at least one header file,
cross-referenced against local_include_dirs. Found 436 missing
directories total. Checked each for filename collisions against both
already-included dirs and other missing dirs (since blindly adding a
colliding directory risks the compiler silently picking the wrong
header -- a correctness bug, not just a build break). 21 are genuine
collisions and were excluded:
- cmrtlib/* vs media_driver/*/cm/* (unrelated libraries, same
  filenames by coincidence)
- gen11/gen12_tgllp legacy kernel_free sources duplicating newer
  Xe_HPG_Base equivalents
- media_driver/linux/ult (googletest unit-test harness, not part of
  the real driver)
- media_softlet/linux/common/os/i915*/include (legacy i915 KMD
  backend; this product uses the xe/ backend)

Added the remaining 415 directories, confirmed collision-free.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
